ted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I do realize that it's mostly an RTFM issue that is obvious for an experience SQLAlchemy user. But I'm not one, and I got stuck with this for quite some time, so I wonder something can be improved here.\r\n\r\nI got derailed from the correct `Query.join` usage after hitting bug #4427, and ended up with:\r\n```\r\n>>> session.query(B).join(B.a_id)\r\n...\r\n  File \"/home/dtantsur/Projects/temp/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/orm/query.py\", line 2244, in _join\r\n    right_entity = onclause.property.mapper\r\n  File \"/home/dtantsur/Projects/temp/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/util/langhelpers.py\", line 853, in __getattr__\r\n    return self._fallback_getattr(key)\r\n  File \"/home/dtantsur/Projects/temp/lib/python3.7/site-packages/sqlalchemy/util/langhelpers.py\", line 831, in _fallback_getattr\r\n    raise AttributeError(key)\r\nAttributeError: mapper\r\n```\r\nThe same thing with\r\n```\r\n>>> session.query(B).join(A, B.a_id)\r\n```\r\nNow, it does not sound completely unreasonable to me to use a foreign key as a hint for JOIN, but that's not the point here. I wonder if the exception can be caught and the error message be something\r\n```\r\nExpected a mapped object, such as a model or a statement, got a Column.\r\n```","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"